# 25 YEARS OF API ACCESS #

Thank you to Wikipedia for not only making knowledge freely accessible and open for 25 years, but for treating it as something meant to be utilized for the greater good, not just read.

The APIs, open data, and tooling behind the scenes matter just as much as the articles themselves. The API can train smart assistants, enable scientific research, and unlock more creativity than most people ever see. In a web that increasingly locks things down, Wikipedia’s commitment to openness with its front end and back end alike remains extraordinary.  [LINK: (SaladCatPasta) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=User:SaladCatPasta&action=edit&redlink=1]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=User_talk:SaladCatPasta&action=edit&redlink=1] )  [LINK: (03:12, 21 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary#c-SaladCatPasta-20260121031200-25_Years_of_API_access] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary] ]


