# WISHING WIKIPEDIA ANOTHER FABULOUS 25 YEARS #

One of the greatest honors of my life was to work for the  [LINK: (Wikimedia Foundation) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikimedia_Foundation]  and serve (as employee #4!) the thousands of volunteers who have created this wonderful thing. I am so very grateful to have had the pleasure of carrying and sharing the message of  [LINK: (free culture) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_culture]  for all these years. While it is hard to believe it has been 25 years, the value Wikipedia has given the world is undeniable. We must be vigilant in protecting what we have created, and most importantly, not taking it for granted. These uncertain times require steadfast support for freedom of speech, freedom of thought, and reliance on our unshakeable core principles. Truth matters now more than ever. To all my friends near and far, smile and be happy for what we have wrought. I see you! -- [LINK: (Brad Patrick) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:BradPatrick]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:BradPatrick] )  [LINK: (15:21, 21 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary#c-BradPatrick-20260121152100-Wishing_Wikipedia_another_fabulous_25_years] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary] ]


