# HAPPY BDAY WIKIPEDIA #

I grew up hearing teachers say “dont use Wikipedia as a source”. Now, in the days of alternate facts, twitter news, political disinformation and measles, i cant help but think - “you dun goofed”. I’ll never really agree with your stance on what constitutes a good source yourself - your fixation on books - as if the highest selling book of all time doesn't claim women came from the rib of a man. And I won’t always agree on what’s “objective”, on articles about terrible people or ideas. BUT I will always be certain the Wikipedia community is, as a whole, one of the best demographics out there. Unbiased, embracing knowledge, and making progress - no matter who’s “anti woke” sensibilities it offends. You’re a bulwark against the rising tide of first-impression reactivity, dark ages igno-arrogance - from all sides. You are political, because the truth is political.

love ya all, and thank you for your service  [LINK: (~2025-37898-77) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Contributions/~2025-37898-77]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=User_talk:~2025-37898-77&action=edit&redlink=1] )  [LINK: (14:17, 25 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary#c-~2025-37898-77-20260125141700-Happy_bday_Wikipedia] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary] ]


