# TIME, DOCTOR FREEMAN? IS IT REALLY THAT TIME AGAIN? #

It seems as if you only just arrived! (Thank you to those who got where that's from!) Really, though, Wikipedia is older than I am, and yet it really feels like I've gotten to grow up alongside this platform! I remember scrolling endlessly through articles on my school laptop in Middle School, and advocating for its usefulness as a source of knowledge. Man, I got teased for that a lot, heh. Anyway, happy incredible birthday to this incredible platform! I only hope that, in another 25 years, I'll be right here, writing yet another crappy reference!  [LINK: (Trotg) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Trotg]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:Trotg] )  [LINK: (17:16, 27 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary#c-Trotg-20260127171600-Time,_Doctor_Freeman?_Is_it_really_that_time_again?] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary] ]


