# HAPPY BIRTHDAY WIKIPEDIA #

This is one of the best websites ever, and perhaps the best educational resource ever. I (and many other people) know so much because of Wikipedia, and I can gladly say that the total amount of time I've spent on here reading articles probably amounts to at least 24 hours or longer. I don't think I've ever gotten bored reading articles, and I find most articles to be wonderful and beautiful. Many articles have been around for at least a decade and have gone through TONS of changes, and their revision histories beautifully reflect the combined effort of everybody who cared enough to edit, and formulate one great article that is consistent in style with the rest of the articles. The articles are simply works of art in that regard.  [LINK: (JeffTheMasterr) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:JeffTheMasterr]  ( [LINK: (talk) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/User_talk:JeffTheMasterr] )  [LINK: (01:47, 30 January 2026 (UTC)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary#c-JeffTheMasterr-20260130014700-HAPPY_BIRTHDAY_WIKIPEDIA_23] [ [LINK: (reply) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:25th_anniversary] ]


